players new gameplay options because if  a silenced weapon was portrayed as being  almost as loud as a non silenced weapon  you're taking away choice and player  agency and interesting gameplay variety  as I'm sure you can imagine sneaking  around outer Haven a snake would be much  less fun without a silencer Sam Fisher  probably wouldn't be shooting out lights  if each gunshot was echoing around  whatever location he's trying to sneak  into and agent 47 would have been shot  long before anyone could sully his good  name with lackluster film adaptations  but not all games are shoe realism  Sumpter the line of that realism and put  a lot of work into making sure their  virtual firearms look and feel authentic  I took some virtual firing ranges to see  how different games handled suppressors  I'm a three being a game that's  applauded for its realism still mutes  down some of its weapons but a silenced  rifle especially a higher caliber one  still has a pretty hefty audible report  when fired the modern warfare series has  changed quite significantly when you  measure the whisper-quiet suppressors of  modern warfare to the much louder  suppress gunshots of the 2019 one of  warfare reboot and well in the stealthy  titles of the Hitman series they may as  well be magic another key consideration  for suppressors in video games is how  they impact balance especially in  multiplayer experiences if they were  treated accurately sticking a suppressor  on the end of your rifle or SMG in Call  of Duty would come with very little  downside the noise the gun makes would  be one small benefit with the various  other performance benefits that come  with using a suppressor would make them  unfair in a video game setting and  detract from the potential variety in  gameplay to deal with this silencers are  used to make guns extremely quiet but  also do things like hide the flash from  your weapon and prevent you from  appearing on the mini-map however the  trade-off is often things like decreased  damage lower bullet velocity or reduced  range for your weapon and if you  remember what I said earlier this  wouldn't actually happen in real life at  least not to the degree that exists in  games the impact of suppressors is being  interpreted in a very narrow and  sometimes exaggerated way but I'm kind  of glad that it is as much as I love  feeling the authenticity and accuracy of  guns in games like armored insurgency or  Sniper Elite and appreciate the  attention to detail at those games have  I also really like when there's gameplay  options available to me so that firing  guns in a virtual space feels varied and  interesting  but I don't give a [ __ ] without the  ability to play a little fast and loose  with how suppressors work it's likely  games like hitman or Metal Gear Solid  wouldn't exist as we know them and it  would mean much less varieties available  to you in games like Call of Duty or  battlefield silencers can also do for  players what they do for protagonists  make them feel like a badass which is  sometimes exactly what you need thank  you so much for watching this very  espionage filled episode of loadout if  you enjoyed it hit the like button  subscribe and let your thoughts known in  the comment section down below
 

